{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473418996,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzU5ODM2NzA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/780","origin":"github"},"title":"`create` doesn't support path resolution","message":"```\nmih@meiner /tmp/some (git)-[master] % datalad ls\n.  [annex]  master  - 2016-09-09/12:46:31  OK\nmih@meiner /tmp/some (git)-[master] % mkdir test\nmih@meiner /tmp/some (git)-[master] % cd test\nmih@meiner /tmp/some/test (git)-[master] % datalad create deep\n2016-09-09 12:59:55,433 [INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/some/test/deep (create.py:217)\nCreated dataset at /tmp/some/test/deep.\n```\n\nSo far all good, treats path as relative to CWD. But:\n\n```\nmih@meiner /tmp/some/test (git)-[master] % datalad create -d /tmp/some notthatdeep\nusage: datalad [-h] [-l {critical,error,warning,info,debug,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9}]\n               [-p {condor}] [--version] [--dbg] [--idbg] [-C PATH]\n               {search-datasets,aggregate-metadata,create,install,add,publish,uninstall,update,create-publication-target-sshwebserver,add-sibling,modify-subdataset-urls,unlock,save,test,crawl,crawl-init,ls,clean,add-archive-content,download-url,create-test-dataset}\n               ...\ndatalad: error: unrecognized arguments: -d notthatdeep\n```\n\nIMHO it should also get `-d` now and also support paths that are relative to a given dataset -- if only for consistency.","files":null}]}